  "period_note": "Year-end position from the Annual Report's own multi-year 'Financial Performance at a Glance (Solo)' / 'Financial Highlights (Solo)' summary table (audited), Solo basis. As a Shariah-based Islamic bank, reports 'Investment' rather than conventional 'Loans and Advances', and 'Classified Investments' rather than 'NPL'. Total deposits fell year-over-year (BDT 473,046mn -> BDT 455,195mn) while investments kept growing, pushing the Investment-Deposit ratio to 118.45% — well above the typical <100% norm seen in earlier years — an early liquidity-strain signal preceding the sector-wide S. Alam Group-linked stress that became public in 2024 (outside this bank's locally archived report range, which ends at FY2023).",
